With those two tweaks in place, Prism will:

- Recognize `@helper` as a top‐level directive (and give it the ‘keyword’ colour), and  
- Treat the entire `(name) { … }` that follows as one C#/HTML block instead of “just markup”.

You should now see your `<input placeholder="@Localize.GetLabelHtml("…")" />` and your `@helper TrialHelper(…) { … }` rendering nicely, just like Visual Studio does.
